# Redoubt LW-M3-07: wait for a live blocking response listener before first navigation.
#
# A ready background page is not a filtering-readiness signal: uBO 1.74.0
# starts filters in an asynchronous IIFE and explicitly unsuspends requests
# during first installation. In its pinned start.js/traffic.js, live blocking
# onHeadersReceived registration happens only after filter initialization.
# Track real registrations, not primed persistent listeners; expose a bounded,
# version-bound GeckoView wait without modifying the signed XPI or its trust.
# This API proves listener activation, not arbitrary extension internals.
# UUID-bound cancellation immediately removes timer/listeners and cannot affect
# unrelated requests or a later request reusing a completed identifier.
#
# On every launch after installation (APP_STARTUP) Gecko delays a persistent
# background until the first browser window paints, and the embedder holds
# every window on this wait: nothing starts uBO and each relaunch times out.
# The wait therefore starts a delayed background itself, as install/enable
# and a primed request do, once runManifest() has registered that handler.
# It judges the policy Extension.startup() settles on, not the early stub
# whose permissions are not loaded yet.
#
